Original commit body from 81f55317e191b642cee45954fd2aeacdb5255717:

A cached survey is reused only by runs with the same analysis
configuration: backends (WI-givib) and --trace-deps (WI-bapal) were in
the key, -e/--exclude was not. ``hypergumbo survey repo -e lib`` wrote
over the plain survey of ``repo``, and ``hypergumbo search lo repo``, a
read command the user never asked to exclude anything, then answered
"No symbols found matching lo" from it.

``discovery.exclude_cache_token`` digests the stripped, de-duplicated,
sorted patterns into ``ex-<12 hex>``; ``_get_results_cache_dir`` takes
``extra_excludes`` and suffixes the state segment with it, as the
trace-deps, channel and config tokens are. ``run_survey`` writes under
that key; the ``sketch`` command and ``_discover_or_survey`` read and
auto-run under it, so ``sketch -e lib`` is consistent with itself. Read
commands take no ``--exclude`` and keep the plain key: an excluding
survey is never what they find, the same rule as a one-off backend
flag.

Red: the item's three-command repro, run in-process, lost ``lo``.
Green: the plain survey still holds ``hi`` and ``lo``; the excluding
survey lives under its own key with ``hi`` only. A sketch test's stub
of the cache-dir function gains the keyword the real one now takes.

